  "notes": [
    "A balance chain (the owner's decision of 6 Oct 2026): read-v6's chain-balances reads it only when a request asks for it (`tokens`). No Domino V2 deployment, index, plan or automation runs here, so it is not a Domino chain profile (api-contracts/v2/chains) and names only what a balance and its qualified USD read.",
    "USDC is Circle's native USDC (0x0b2C639c...), not the bridged USDC.e (0x7F5c764c...), which is priced like any other token, by its pools. Its code hash is the FiatTokenProxy's; decimals() 6 and symbol() USDC at the verification block.",
    "ETH and WETH are priced from Chainlink's ETH / USD feed (path eth-usd: 8 decimals, heartbeat 1,200 s, deviation 0.15%, aggregator 0x16C04812... at the verification block), gated by the L2 sequencer uptime feed with the read path's 3,600 s grace. At the verification block the sequencer answered up (0) since 1783448495.",
    "Pools created before the 11 Nov 2021 regenesis keep CREATE2 addresses of the same init code hash: getPool(WETH, USDC.e, 500) == CREATE2 (0x85149247...) at the verification block, as do the native USDC's WETH pools at 500 and 3000.",
    "The v3 factory enables the four standard tiers only: feeAmountTickSpacing(200), (300) and (400) answered 0 at the verification block (Base alone adds them).",
    "StateView.poolManager() is the PoolManager above at the verification block."
  ],
